n households yes there is  a short-term cost you will know trevor  as the as people go back into work that  cost then diminishes because it's a  means-tested benefit of means-tested  household benefits so people do go back  into higher paying jobs they don't  qualify for it so the cost automatically  comes down but also there are people who  can't work people with serious  disabilities how are they going to get  through this winter that's a huge  problem but crucially as well  in terms of recovering from the pandemic  do we want to take that spending from  local shops and local services every  decision we have to make as a country  will be made harder if we don't come out  of the pandemic  in the best possible way and taking that  money out of local economies i'm afraid  it's the wrong decision for the country
 

